{"type":"text","timestamp":1792504158156,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"id":"prt_15991c84c001J0bxv5Ms7rBAAi","messageID":"msg_1598f5fb70010TORdoJ9Aw1Ygv","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","type":"text","text":"\n\nNow let me implement the candidate. My approach: maintain the ordering plus adjacency bitmasks; after each update, validate the current ordering via the (LB) 4-point property (cheap with bitmasks), keep it if still valid, else recompute a fast bitmask LexBFS.\n\n","time":{"start":1792504088652,"end":1792504158148}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792504158191,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-913ebb2206db8f18","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic LexBFS ordering maintenance (undirected).\n\nMaintains *some* valid LexBFS ordering (any start vertex, any tie-break) under\nedge insertions and deletions. The verifier accepts any ordering that satisfies\nthe (LB) 4-point property of Corneil & Krueger, so after each single-edge flip\nwe first test whether the ordering we already hold is still valid; if it is we\nkeep it (no recompute), otherwise we recompute a fresh ordering.\n\nState (a plain dict, JSON-serialisable):\n  'ordering': list of the n vertex ids in the maintained LexBFS order\n  'adj':      list of n ints; adj[u] is a bitmask with bit v set iff u~v\n\nAdjacency is kept as bitmasks so both the validity test and the recompute are\ncheap (bit ops), well below the offline partition-refinement baseline.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(n, adj):\n    \"\"\"Partition-refinement LexBFS over adjacency bitmasks.\n\n    Starts at vertex 0 with the increasing-id tie-break. Returns the ordering.\n    \"\"\"\n    order = []\n    # Pi is a list of cells; each cell is a list of vertices in current order.\n    Pi = [list(range(n))]\n    while len(order) < n:\n        p = Pi[0][0]\n        order.append(p)\n        neigh = adj[p]\n        newPi = []\n        for C in Pi:\n            a = [v for v in C if v != p and ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            b = [v for v in C if v != p and not ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            if a:\n                newPi.append(a)\n            if b:\n                newPi.append(b)\n        Pi = newPi\n    return order\n\n\ndef _lb_valid(ordering, adj, n):\n    \"\"\"Return True iff `ordering` satisfies the (LB) 4-point property.\n\n    (LB): for all positions a < b < c with ac in E and ab not in E, there is a\n    d at position < a with db in E and dc not in E.\n\n    prefix[a] is the bitmask of the vertices at positions < a; sep(vb, vc) is\n    the bitmask of vertices d with db in E and dc not in E. The witness exists\n    before position a iff prefix[a] & sep(vb, vc) is non-zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    prefix = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] | (1 << ordering[i])\n\n    sep_cache = {}\n\n    def sep(vb, vc):\n        s = sep_cache.get((vb, vc))\n        if s is None:\n            s = 0\n            for d in range(n):\n                if ((adj[d] >> vb) & 1) and not ((adj[d] >> vc) & 1):\n                    s |= 1 << d\n            sep_cache[(vb, vc)] = s\n        return s\n\n    for a in range(n):\n        va = ordering[a]\n        va_adj = adj[va]\n        for b in range(a + 1, n):\n            vb = ordering[b]\n            if (va_adj >> vb) & 1:\n                continue  # ab in E: (LB) does not constrain this triple\n            for c in range(b + 1, n):\n                vc = ordering[c]\n                if not ((va_adj >> vc) & 1):\n                    continue  # ac not in E\n                if not (prefix[a] & sep(vb, vc)):\n                    return False  # no separating witness before a\n    return True\n\n\ndef _build(n, adj):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(n, adj), \"adj\": adj}\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    adj = [0] * n\n    for u in range(n):\n        row = graph[u]\n        mask = 0\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v]:\n                mask |= 1 << v\n        adj[u] = mask\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] |= 1 << v\n    adj[v] |= 1 << u\n    if _lb_valid(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] &= ~(1 << v)\n    adj[v] &= ~(1 << u)\n    if _lb_valid(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792504158133,"end":1792504158183}},"id":"prt_15991cbe8001rvhoGbfpZRK57i","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","messageID":"msg_1598f5fb70010TORdoJ9Aw1Ygv"}}
