{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792504751585,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"id":"prt_1599be5cc0015d5KoYX1omNsYn","messageID":"msg_1599be2dc001xKgm5rZbPwEkbX","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","snapshot":"4049d664845d352e4e2d1202a718f2ec63b7a966","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792504902209,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"id":"prt_1599de7a1001kdxEoH4eoI116r","messageID":"msg_1599be2dc001xKgm5rZbPwEkbX","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe validate step (O(n³)) costs about as much as a recompute, so it's not paying off. The fix: **localize the validity check to only the triples affected by the flipped edge** (O(n²)), since a single edge flip can only change the status of triples where at least one of {a,b,c} is the flipped endpoint. Let me verify this reasoning is sound, then implement.\n\nMy proof: a triple (a,b,c) with a<b<c can change (LB) status only if (i) edge ac flipped, (ii) edge ab flipped, or (iii) the witness set W(b,c)={d: b~d, ¬c~d} changed. Each of these requires at least one of {a,b,c} to be a flipped endpoint u or v. Conversely, if none of {a,b,c} is u or v, then ac, ab, and W(b,c) are all unchanged, so the triple's status is unchanged. So rechecking exactly the triples with b∈{u,v} or c∈{u,v} (a safe superset) is both sound and complete.\n\n","time":{"start":1792504883105,"end":1792504902201}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792504902247,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-964a813d4eee106c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Dynamic LexBFS ordering maintenance (undirected).\n\nMaintains *some* valid LexBFS ordering (any start vertex, any tie-break) under\nedge insertions and deletions. The verifier accepts any ordering that satisfies\nthe (LB) 4-point property of Corneil & Krueger, so after each single-edge flip\nwe first test whether the ordering we already hold is still valid; if it is we\nkeep it (no recompute), otherwise we recompute a fresh ordering.\n\nState (a plain dict, JSON-serialisable):\n  'ordering': list of the n vertex ids in the maintained LexBFS order\n  'adj':      list of n ints; adj[u] is a bitmask with bit v set iff u~v\n\nValidity after a single flip (u, v) is checked *locally*: a triple (a, b, c)\nwith a<b<c can only change its (LB) status if at least one of {a, b, c} is a\nflipped endpoint, because the three things (LB) looks at for that triple --\nwhether ac in E, whether ab in E, and the witness set W(b, c) = {d: b~d, not\nc~d} -- all depend only on edges incident to a, b or c. So we recheck only the\ntriples with b in {u, v} or c in {u, v}, which is O(n^2) instead of O(n^3).\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(n, adj):\n    \"\"\"Partition-refinement LexBFS over adjacency bitmasks.\n\n    Starts at vertex 0 with the increasing-id tie-break. Returns the ordering.\n    \"\"\"\n    order = []\n    # Pi is a list of cells; each cell is a list of vertices in current order.\n    Pi = [list(range(n))]\n    while len(order) < n:\n        p = Pi[0][0]\n        order.append(p)\n        neigh = adj[p]\n        newPi = []\n        for C in Pi:\n            a = [v for v in C if v != p and ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            b = [v for v in C if v != p and not ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            if a:\n                newPi.append(a)\n            if b:\n                newPi.append(b)\n        Pi = newPi\n    return order\n\n\ndef _sep_mask(adj, n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"Bitmask of vertices d with x~d and not y~d (the witness set for pair (x, y)).\"\"\"\n    s = 0\n    for d in range(n):\n        if ((adj[d] >> x) & 1) and not ((adj[d] >> y) & 1):\n            s |= 1 << d\n    return s\n\n\ndef _lb_valid_after_flip(ordering, adj, n, u, v):\n    \"\"\"Return True iff `ordering` still satisfies (LB) after flipping edge (u, v).\n\n    Rechecks only triples (a, b, c) with b in {u, v} or c in {u, v}; every other\n    triple has unchanged (ac in E), (ab in E) and witness set, so its (LB)\n    status is unchanged from the previously valid state.\n    \"\"\"\n    # prefix[i] = bitmask of the vertices at positions < i\n    prefix = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] | (1 << ordering[i])\n\n    # Witness masks for every pair where at least one endpoint is u or v.\n    sep = {}\n    for x in (u, v):\n        for y in range(n):\n            if y != x:\n                sep[(x, y)] = _sep_mask(adj, n, x, y)\n                sep[(y, x)] = _sep_mask(adj, n, y, x)\n\n    for b in range(n):\n        for c in range(b + 1, n):\n            if b not in (u, v) and c not in (u, v):\n                continue  # no triple (a, b, c) is affected\n            sbc = sep.get((b, c))\n            for a in range(b):\n                va = ordering[a]\n                va_adj = adj[va]\n                vb = ordering[b]\n                vc = ordering[c]\n                if ((va_adj >> vc) & 1) and not ((va_adj >> vb) & 1):\n                    # ac in E, ab not in E: need a witness d at position < a\n                    if sbc is None:\n                        sbc = _sep_mask(adj, n, b, c)\n                    if not (prefix[a] & sbc):\n                        return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef _build(n, adj):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(n, adj), \"adj\": adj}\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    adj = [0] * n\n    for u in range(n):\n        row = graph[u]\n        mask = 0\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v]:\n                mask |= 1 << v\n        adj[u] = mask\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] |= 1 << v\n    adj[v] |= 1 << u\n    if _lb_valid_after_flip(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n, u, v):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] &= ~(1 << v)\n    adj[v] &= ~(1 << u)\n    if _lb_valid_after_flip(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n, u, v):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n","filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792504902185,"end":1792504902237}},"id":"prt_1599df32f001Nt2ojpVRwLD1yw","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","messageID":"msg_1599be2dc001xKgm5rZbPwEkbX"}}
