{"type":"text","timestamp":1792505014349,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"id":"prt_1599fcf25001J8tFxzJuJFelIb","messageID":"msg_1599ed41e001mMjg9gnP8oXiS6","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","type":"text","text":"\n\nFound the bug: I was comparing **position** indices `b, c` against the flipped **vertex** ids `u, v`, instead of the vertices `ordering[b]`, `ordering[c]`. The skip condition must test the vertices at those positions. Let me fix it.\n\n","time":{"start":1792505007910,"end":1792505014342}}}
