{"type":"text","timestamp":1792505252588,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"id":"prt_159a3610c001AzsTZGcjUtr1O9","messageID":"msg_159a1984b001sLUR4gUNDrPqZv","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe local check's constant is too high (tuple membership + dict precompute) — it's actually 6× slower than the O(n³) full check at n≤4. But I found a much better lever: the witness set `W(b,c) = {d: b~d, ¬c~d}` is exactly `N(b) \\ N(c) = adj[b] & ~adj[c]` as a bitmask — **O(1)**, no per-`d` loop and no dict. That makes the full (LB) check's inner test a few bit ops. Let me rewrite with this.\n\n","time":{"start":1792505241868,"end":1792505252581}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792505253331,"sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a9089bef10bccd7a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Dynamic LexBFS ordering maintenance (undirected).\n\nMaintains *some* valid LexBFS ordering (any start vertex, any tie-break) under\nedge insertions and deletions. The verifier accepts any ordering that satisfies\nthe (LB) 4-point property of Corneil & Krueger, so after each single-edge flip\nwe first test whether the ordering we already hold is still valid; if it is we\nkeep it (no recompute), otherwise we recompute a fresh ordering.\n\nState (a plain dict, JSON-serialisable):\n  'ordering': list of the n vertex ids in the maintained LexBFS order\n  'adj':      list of n ints; adj[u] is a bitmask with bit v set iff u~v\n\nThe (LB) test uses the identity that the witness set of a pair (b, c),\n  W(b, c) = { d : b~d and not c~d },\nis exactly N(b) \\\\ N(c) = adj[b] & ~adj[c] (a bitmask), so each (LB) triple\ntest is a handful of bit operations.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _lexbfs(n, adj):\n    \"\"\"Partition-refinement LexBFS over adjacency bitmasks.\n\n    Starts at vertex 0 with the increasing-id tie-break. Returns the ordering.\n    \"\"\"\n    order = []\n    # Pi is a list of cells; each cell is a list of vertices in current order.\n    Pi = [list(range(n))]\n    while len(order) < n:\n        p = Pi[0][0]\n        order.append(p)\n        neigh = adj[p]\n        newPi = []\n        for C in Pi:\n            a = [v for v in C if v != p and ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            b = [v for v in C if v != p and not ((neigh >> v) & 1)]\n            if a:\n                newPi.append(a)\n            if b:\n                newPi.append(b)\n        Pi = newPi\n    return order\n\n\ndef _lb_valid(ordering, adj, n):\n    \"\"\"Return True iff `ordering` satisfies the (LB) 4-point property.\n\n    (LB): for all positions a < b < c with ac in E and ab not in E, there is a\n    d at position < a with db in E and dc not in E.\n\n    prefix[a] is the bitmask of the vertices at positions < a. The witness set\n    W(b, c) = N(b) \\\\ N(c) = adj[b] & ~adj[c], so the witness exists before\n    position a iff prefix[a] & (adj[b] & ~adj[c]) is non-zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    prefix = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] | (1 << ordering[i])\n\n    for a in range(n):\n        va = ordering[a]\n        va_adj = adj[va]\n        pa = prefix[a]\n        for b in range(a + 1, n):\n            vb = ordering[b]\n            if (va_adj >> vb) & 1:\n                continue  # ab in E: (LB) does not constrain this triple\n            vb_adj = adj[vb]\n            for c in range(b + 1, n):\n                vc = ordering[c]\n                if not ((va_adj >> vc) & 1):\n                    continue  # ac not in E\n                if not (pa & (vb_adj & ~adj[vc])):\n                    return False  # no separating witness before a\n    return True\n\n\ndef _build(n, adj):\n    return {\"ordering\": _lexbfs(n, adj), \"adj\": adj}\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    adj = [0] * n\n    for u in range(n):\n        row = graph[u]\n        mask = 0\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v]:\n                mask |= 1 << v\n        adj[u] = mask\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] |= 1 << v\n    adj[v] |= 1 << u\n    if _lb_valid(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    n = len(state[\"adj\"])\n    adj = state[\"adj\"]\n    adj[u] &= ~(1 << v)\n    adj[v] &= ~(1 << u)\n    if _lb_valid(state[\"ordering\"], adj, n):\n        return state\n    return _build(n, adj)\n","filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_lbfs_s1/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792505252569,"end":1792505253323}},"id":"prt_159a36714001MLTuVJrppG6bWk","sessionID":"ses_ea67781bcffe0HPBy9O3ZA3rA8","messageID":"msg_159a1984b001sLUR4gUNDrPqZv"}}
